# Infrastructure

Terraform-managed Cloudflare and GitHub infrastructure for `{{ github_org }}` ({% if backend == 'hcp' %}state and runs in HCP Terraform{% else %}state in {{ state_backend }} object storage, CI in GitHub Actions{% endif %}), generated
from [copier-infra](https://github.com/hasansezertasan/copier-infra) and designed to be
maintained with [infra-copilot](https://github.com/hasansezertasan/infra-copilot).

## Start here

1. Install infra-copilot using its current installation instructions.
2. Ask your agent to use infra-copilot to finish setup ({% if backend == 'hcp' %}HCP workspaces, credentials as
   sensitive workspace variables, VCS-driven plans{% else %}the state bucket, plan and apply workflows, GitHub Apps and the `production` environment{% endif %}).
3. Pull template changes later with `copier update`.

Do not commit credentials. Public deployment identifiers live in
`.infra-copilot/config.md`, rendered from `.copier-answers.yml`; API tokens and GitHub App
credentials belong only in {% if backend == 'hcp' %}the corresponding HCP Terraform workspace{% else %}GitHub Actions secrets, with apply credentials only in the `production` environment{% endif %}.

## Shape

Each directory below is an independent Terraform root with its own state and provider
lock file:

| Directory | {% if backend == 'hcp' %}HCP workspace{% else %}State prefix{% endif %} | Initial responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| `terraform/cloudflare` | `{% if backend == 'hcp' %}cloudflare{% else %}{{ state_prefix }}/cloudflare{% endif %}` | Verify access to the configured Cloudflare zone |
| `terraform/github` | `{% if backend == 'hcp' %}github-org{% else %}{{ state_prefix }}/github{% endif %}` | Verify access to the configured GitHub repositories |

The initial data sources are read-only credential probes. Add managed resources with
infra-copilot after setup. If a resource already exists, import it before applying.

## Development

Review `mise.toml` before trusting it, then install the committed toolchain:

```sh
mise trust mise.toml
MISE_LOCKED=1 mise install terraform gh jq
mise exec -- make check
```

{% if backend == 'hcp' -%}
HCP Terraform creates plans through its VCS integration. GitHub Actions runs only
credential-free formatting, validation, and contract checks. Applies require manual
confirmation in HCP Terraform.
{%- else -%}
`ci.yml` runs credential-free formatting, validation, and contract checks. The plan and
apply workflows are added by infra-copilot's setup; applies run from `main` in the
`production` environment.
{%- endif %}
